        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on incident scenarios, scope, and playbook structure.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 409854,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, kicking off the Crisis Communication Playbook project. First step is to align on the scope. I've started a doc to brainstorm the key incident scenarios we need to cover. Let's get our thoughts in there so we can finalize the list. This will feed into T1.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "wave",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 47537,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Great start. I've added three common ones to the doc: physical altercation, unauthorized access, and medical emergency. I think we should also consider a fire/evacuation scenario. We need to keep the list focused for v1.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 143124,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Good list. We should also consider the nuance between an internal-only incident versus one with immediate external visibility. For example, a contained chemical spill versus a major fire visible from off-site. The communication chain and messaging needs will differ significantly based on public impact.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 47290,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "what about a theft? we had that happen once.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 286680,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "That's a good point. Maybe we can have a severity scale for each type.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 47537,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "Let's keep it simple for now to avoid scope creep. How about we agree on these five for v1: 1. Physical Altercation, 2. Unauthorized Access/Intrusion, 3. Medical Emergency, 4. Fire/Evacuation, 5. On-site protest/demonstration. We can add theft as a subset of #2. Does that work for everyone?",
            "mentions": [
              47290,
              143124,
              409854,
              286680
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 409854,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "Works for me. That's a solid, manageable list. I've updated the T1 ticket description to reflect this. Decision locked.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 47290,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "ok",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 409854,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "Next, let's talk structure. For T2, I'm proposing a simple structure for the playbook: 1. Intro & Roles, 2. Incident-Specific Checklists, 3. Communication Templates (Internal/External), 4. Media Handling Guide, 5. Post-Incident Review. Thoughts?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 143124,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "The structure is logical. For the 'Roles' section, we must be extremely clear on the RACI, especially the handoff points between on-site security, the comms team, and legal. The A8 Stakeholder Matrix is a good starting point, but we need to map it to actions within the playbook itself.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 286680,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "I agree with the structure. Who is owning which section?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 47537,
            "reply_to": "M11",
            "text": "Good question. Based on the backlog, it looks like this: Checklists (T3, T8) would be led by a spokesperson. Templates (T4, T5) split between PR and myself. Media Guide (T7) is PR. Does that sound right? We can formalize this in the T2 ownership matrix.",
            "mentions": [
