        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Define on-site escalation scripts and quick-reference checklists.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 286680,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi all, here is a first look at the escalation script for on-site staff, as part of T3. Let me know what you think.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 47290,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "When I was a guard we just called the supervisor on the radio. Is that in here?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 47537,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Thanks for getting this started. I have a few thoughts to make it more user-friendly under pressure. I think we should reformat this as a simple checklist, maybe using bullet points and bold keywords. For example: '1. ASSESS immediate danger. 2. REPORT to site supervisor with code word. 3. SECURE the area.' We need language that's impossible to misinterpret. This connects to T8 for the one-page checklists.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 409854,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "I love that suggestion. A clear, numbered checklist is exactly what's needed. We should also include the direct phone number for the 24/7 operations center right at the top. Let's make this the official On-Site Incident Escalation Checklist, A2.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 286680,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "Ok, that makes sense. I can reformat it as a checklist.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 143124,
            "reply_to": "M22",
            "text": "From a legal standpoint, the language needs to be precise without being prescriptive about actions that could introduce liability. 'Secure the area' is good, but we should add 'if safe to do so'. We need to ensure the script doesn't conflict with their formal safety training.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 47537,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "Excellent point. Safety first. I've taken all the feedback and created a revised version in a new doc, incorporating the checklist format, contact info, and the safety caveats. Please take a look. If we're happy with this, we can approve it.",
            "mentions": [
              286680,
